<article class="env-definition" id="08RP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08RP">Definition <span data-tag="08RP">17.28.3</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a topological space. Let $\varphi : \mathcal{O}_1 \to \mathcal{O}_2$ be a homomorphism of sheaves of rings on $X$. The <em>module of differentials</em> of $\varphi $ is the object representing the functor $\mathcal{F} \mapsto \text{Der}_{\mathcal{O}_1}(\mathcal{O}_2, \mathcal{F})$ which exists by Lemma <a href="/tag/08RM" data-tag="08RM">17.28.2</a>. It is denoted $\Omega _{\mathcal{O}_2/\mathcal{O}_1}$, and the <em>universal $\varphi $-derivation</em> is denoted $\text{d} : \mathcal{O}_2 \to \Omega _{\mathcal{O}_2/\mathcal{O}_1}$. </p>
</article>